 "notes": "ACCESS: bedbathandbeyond.com is now Beyond Inc.'s (ex-Overstock) marketplace catalogue. Direct fetches of /c/ listing pages are Akamai 403; per notes/44.md the only working route is translate.goog (www-bedbathandbeyond-com.translate.goog/<path>?_x_tr_sl=en&_x_tr_tl=es&_x_tr_hl=en), which returns genuine server-rendered origin HTML. It worked again this session (occasional HTTP 429 from Google, cleared on retry with backoff). All link values are canonical bedbathandbeyond.com origin URLs.\nTREE: taken from the site's own taxonomy, not from link scraping. The Furniture tier-1 page /c/furniture?t=24352 carries __NEXT_DATA__ pageData.document.leftNav (Bedroom, Dining, Kitchen, Bar, Living Room, Bathroom, Home Office, Kids Bedroom & Nursery, Mattresses, Patio) and the mega-menu adds two more Furniture-department tier-2s not in leftNav: Entryway Furniture (t=24399) and Game Room Furniture (t=31265). Every listing page carries facets[attributeGroupId='categories'].values, i.e. the site's own child-category list with canonical URLs; I walked that recursively (178 nodes reached, all HTTP 200). I additionally walked three genuine furniture nodes that sit outside the Furniture department: Storage Furniture (t=31351, under Storage & Organization), Baby Furniture (t=19426) and Kids Playroom Furniture (t=31079). I did NOT enumerate the rest of this very large marketplace.\nCOUNTS: each page server-renders three agreeing signals - the visible header, __NEXT_DATA__ pageData.resultCount, and JSON-LD ItemList numberOfItems. Across all 178 walked nodes the rendered header matched resultCount exactly on 147 and was display-capped as '5,000+' on the other 31 (all of them >5000); ZERO mismatches. So evidence quotes the rendered header wherever it is not capped, and cites resultCount (noting the cap) for the 5,000+ ones. Exhaustion check on Baker's Racks (reported 298): &page=1..5 returned 60/60/60/60/58 = 298 slots and &page=6 fell back to page 1, confirming the reported total is where pagination actually ends (the union of unique IDs was 288 because 10 items reshuffled between page requests). Tile counting was deliberately NOT used: every page's products array carries 81 entries, 60 real plus a 21-item next-page prefetch (the Beyond/Overstock trap in notes/44.md). Drift check: Sofas, Dining Tables, Adirondack Chairs, Hall Trees and Cribs were re-read fresh later in the session and all five returned identical numbers. Facet counts (parent's view of a child) run a little behind the child page's own resultCount (e.g. Living Room Seating 31209 vs 31353) - I always used the child page's own number, never a facet count and never a parent's number.\nDEDUPE: this taxonomy is a graph, not a tree - many nodes hang off several parents (Bookshelves under both Living Room and Home Office; Bedroom Sets under both Bedroom Furniture and Beds & Headboards; Outdoor Dining Sets under both Patio Furniture Sets and Outdoor Dining Furniture; almost all of Storage Furniture's children duplicate Bedroom/Dining/Office nodes). Each taxonomy id is emitted exactly once, under its most natural parent. 'Patio Furniture Sets' and 'Kids Storage' were dropped as grouping rows because every one of their children was already emitted elsewhere or excluded.\nEXCLUDED (all deliberate): Mattresses department and Crib & Toddler Mattresses (bedding, per brief); Indoor Fireplaces (heating appliance); Living Room Furniture Accessories and its slipcover/cushion children, Home Office Furniture Accessories (chair mats/supports), Patio Furniture Accessories (outdoor cushions, throw pillows, umbrellas, umbrella bases, furniture covers) - all furniture covers/parts/textiles; Laptop Stands; Wall Hooks and Bathroom Wall Shelves (wall-mounted, Wall Decor's domain); Umbrella Stands; Wine Racks were KEPT (page-1 titles are freestanding wine cabinets/bar cabinets under the site's Bar Furniture node); Storage Trunks (184) dropped after a title scan showed wicker/decorative storage trunks, i.e. standalone storage goods; Toy Boxes, Kids' Storage Bins, Play Kitchens, Playhouses, Dollhouses, Climbers, Kids' Easels, Playards & Playpens (toys/baby gear); Arcade Games (machines, not tables).\nKEPT AFTER A TITLE CHECK: Massage Chairs and Theater Seating (power-lift recliners), Coat Racks (freestanding coat trees), Shower Stools (teak shower benches/stools), Over-the-Toilet Storage (freestanding bathroom cabinets), Shoe Storage (shoe cabinets), Storage Ottomans, Storage Benches, Game Tables (pool/poker/shuffleboard tables). Two rows carry MANUAL REVIEW flags: Jewelry Armoires (mix of standing armoires and tabletop jewelry boxes) and Cube Shelving (mostly freestanding cube organiser units, some fabric bins).",
